      "id": "no_projection_must_not_grant_via_an_empty_stand_in",
      "note": "§6.1.8 availability rule 1 — THE FAIL-OPEN GUARD, and the case that actually discriminates. `check()` is public API and may be called with no projection. An implementation that substitutes an EMPTY KEY SET finds `has_none_of` SATISFIED, matches the rule and returns allow. UNEVALUABLE is the only reading that refuses. Pass `arguments: null` as NO PROJECTION AT ALL — not an empty object, which is a different case (§6.1.8 rule 2).",
      "default_effect": "deny",
      "rules": [
